From: yasoteien <263659156+yasoteien@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: Fall back to PIO when the DMA init fails on resume

If the DMA cannot be set up again on resume, log it and carry on
without DMA, as at probe (dw_mci_init_dma). Failing the resume
instead leaves a board whose root file system is on the SD card
without its root.

Signed-off-by: yasoteien <263659156+yasoteien@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
index cf5cecc5491d..555b7c09f734 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -3463,10 +3463,15 @@ int dw_mci_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	if (host->use_dma && host->dma_ops->init) {
-		ret = host->dma_ops->init(host);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+	if (host->use_dma && host->dma_ops->init && host->dma_ops->init(host)) {
+		/*
+		 * As at probe (dw_mci_init_dma): carry on without DMA.  Failing
+		 * the resume instead leaves a board whose root file system is on
+		 * the card without its root.
+		 */
+		dev_err(host->dev, "%s: Unable to initialize DMA Controller, using PIO.\n",
+			__func__);
+		host->use_dma = TRANS_MODE_PIO;
 	}
 
 	/*
